Total:216

But any pluses gained (from magic items/study/exercise/whatever) apply 
equally across the range. A +1 ring of Increase Dexterity will change a 
Dexterity of 16 to a 17 just as easily as it changes a 10 to an 11.

So? The result of this 'flat' application of modifiers to the bell curve is 
that it becomes ridiculously easy to max out scores. The value (and penalty) 
that comes from high(low) scores is trivialized.

YANI: Use chance weight as the necessary plusses to get the next level. To 
do this, move the chance numbers half-way down the column, like so:

